         measured: Phi~ + Psi~ = Phi + Psi; the c-terms cancel IDENTICALLY; residual = 0; and at all orders in c the sum rescales only as (1+c)(Phi+Psi), never adding a scalar potential
         reading : this is L241's conformal cancellation re-derived in the bimetric frame, and it is EXACT ALGEBRA, not a regime statement: the conformal lever C(X) carries the matter FORCE (through Phi~, B3) but contributes IDENTICALLY ZERO to the lensing sum, for any shape of C.  The MOND boost that drives rotation curves is invisible to light at the frame level
